    {
      "section": "article.story-header",
      "variant": "default",
      "content": {
        "logo": {
          "assetRole": "customer.logo",
          "alt": "Basalt Health",
          "ref": "/assets/marquee/logo-7.svg"
        },
        "title": "Basalt Health unifies clinical and operational reporting",
        "stats": [
          {
            "value": "24",
            "label": "hospitals on one tested capacity model"
          },
          {
            "value": "45%",
            "label": "faster monthly reporting"
          },
          {
            "value": "1",
            "label": "shared definition of an available bed"
          }
        ],
        "quote": "Clinical and finance teams were reading different bed counts in the same meeting. One governed model now feeds both, with tests on every load, so we talk about patient flow instead of whose numbers are right.",
        "name": "Dr. Mei Lin",
        "role": "Director, Clinical Informatics"
      },
      "motion": {
        "pattern": "stroke.draw-on",
        "reducedMotionFallback": "render-final-state"
      },
      "style": {
        "strokeShape": "stroke.s10",
        "strokeGradient": "gradient.01"
      }
    },
    {
      "section": "article.story-body",
      "variant": "default",
      "content": {
        "meta": {
          "logo": {
            "assetRole": "customer.logo",
            "alt": "Basalt Health",
            "ref": "/assets/marquee/logo-7.svg"
          },
          "facts": [
            {
              "label": "Industry",
              "value": "Healthcare"
            },
            {
              "label": "Headquarters",
              "value": "Melbourne, Australia"
            },
            {
              "label": "Data platform and tools used",
              "value": "Helixa, Lattice, Lattice catalog"
            }
          ]
        },
        "blocks": [
          {
            "kind": "h3",
            "text": "Two teams, two bed counts"
          },
          {
            "kind": "p",
            "text": "Basalt Health runs twenty-four hospitals and a network of community clinics. Its clinical and finance teams both report on capacity, but for years they built those reports separately, from different extracts and with different rules."
          },
          {
            "kind": "p",
            "text": "In planning meetings that meant two numbers for available beds, and a long discussion about which one was right before any real decision could be made."
          },
          {
            "kind": "p",
            "text": "Both teams were doing careful, honest work. The problem was that nobody had ever written down what a bed meant, so each team had quietly settled on the definition that suited its own reporting needs."
          },
          {
            "kind": "h3",
            "text": "Why the numbers disagreed"
          },
          {
            "kind": "p",
            "text": "The differences were not mistakes so much as unwritten assumptions. Clinical reports counted beds that were staffed; finance counted beds that were funded. Neither definition was written down anywhere."
          },
          {
            "kind": "ul",
            "items": [
              {
                "text": "Different extracts taken at different times of day."
              },
              {
                "text": "Different rules for beds closed for cleaning."
              },
              {
                "text": "No shared record of who owned which figure."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "kind": "h3",
            "text": "One model, owned together"
          },
          {
            "kind": "p",
            "text": "Basalt rebuilt capacity reporting as a single Lattice project owned jointly by clinical informatics and finance. Both definitions of a bed were kept, but named, documented and calculated from the same source data."
          },
          {
            "kind": "p",
            "text": "Every load is now tested: bed counts never negative, every ward mapped to one hospital, every hospital reporting every hour."
          },
          {
            "kind": "p",
            "text": "Joint ownership was a deliberate choice. Every change to the capacity model needs one approval from clinical informatics and one from finance, which keeps both teams involved in every decision."
          },
          {
            "kind": "h3",
            "text": "Privacy built into the project"
          },
          {
            "kind": "p",
            "text": "Patient-level data stays in tightly controlled staging models. Everything downstream works with aggregated counts, and access rules are part of the project configuration, reviewed like any other change."
          },
          {
            "kind": "ul",
            "items": [
              {
                "text": "Patient identifiers removed at the staging layer."
              },
              {
                "text": "Access to staging limited to a small, audited group."
              },
              {
                "text": "Every change to access rules goes through review."
              },
              {
                "text": "Quarterly audit of who can see what."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "kind": "h3",
            "text": "Results"
          },
          {
            "kind": "p",
            "text": "Monthly capacity reporting is now forty-five percent faster to produce, and planning meetings start from a single set of figures."
          },
          {
            "kind": "p",
            "text": "The catalog has become the place clinicians and finance staff look up what a figure means before asking the data team."
          },
          {
            "kind": "h3",
            "text": "Reporting that keeps up with the wards"
          },
          {
            "kind": "p",
            "text": "Hourly freshness rules mean bed availability is updated through the day, not just overnight. Ward managers use the same figures as the executive team."
          },
          {
            "kind": "ul",
            "items": [
              {
                "text": "Hourly capacity updates for every hospital."
              },
              {
                "text": "Alerts to ward owners when data is late."
              },
              {
                "text": "One dashboard for clinical and finance leaders."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "kind": "h3",
            "text": "What is next"
          },
          {
            "kind": "p",
            "text": "Basalt is extending the same approach to theatre scheduling and outpatient waiting lists, starting with written definitions agreed by clinical and operational leads."
          },
          {
            "kind": "p",
            "text": "“Writing the definitions down was the hardest part,” says Dr. Mei Lin. “Everything after that was engineering.”"
          },
          {
            "kind": "p",
            "text": "The team has also started training clinical staff to read the catalog and the model descriptions, so that questions about definitions can be answered without a meeting."
          }
        ]
      },
      "motion": {
        "pattern": "static",
        "reducedMotionFallback": "none-needed"
      },
      "style": {
        "chapterLevel": "h3"
      }
    },
    {
